From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] query_cache: EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING keeps fence-flagged reports pending until
 their fence runs

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series), off unless EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1 is set.
Port of Lichii PR 337, 0f0720d07d (Inc0rporate), open upstream.

At Low accuracy, which Ocarina runs use (fast_gpu in the game's settings), CounterReport treats a
fence-flagged report as synchronized: it frees the query at once, and SignalFence may skip the
report's fence as empty and run its operation at once, before the host GPU has run the work the
report follows. Inc0rporate
reports that Ocarina then reads wrong reports and draws white flashes on leaves and walls, and that
this change removes them on an RX 9070 XT, at about the frame time of Default fences.

With the switch these reports go the way Balanced takes them: the query stays registered until its
fence runs, and that one fence is made even when empty. Other fences are skipped as before. Only a
report with unsynced queries gets a real wait: with no other work the fence is a stub and the
operation still runs without waiting for the GPU, as at High and upstream. Report writes also move
to the fence thread. The upstream patch removes is_synced; here the switch turns it off, so T42's
code stays as it is.

Risk: Inc0rporate saw a hang while loading with only the fence half, and felipecsl reports no change
from the other half alone (Intel, on PR 215). This has both, on a tree that also has our split
fixes, and it may stall where the upstream tree does not. Compute release semaphores wait for the
fence too, which adds latency with the window at 500 us. Use EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1 on the first run.
Unset, nothing changes. Not built, not run.
---
 src/video_core/fence_manager.h |  9 ++++++++-
 src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h | 11 ++++++++++-
 src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/fence_manager.h b/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
index 6bbfe0b..36384ad 100644
--- a/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
+++ b/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
@@ -83,7 +83,14 @@ public:
 
     void SignalFence(std::function<void()>&& func) {
         Nx2Profile::Scope profile_scope{Nx2Profile::Zone::Fence};
-        const bool delay_fence = Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorDefault() ? Settings::IsGPULevelHigh() : Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorBalanced() || Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate();
+        // EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1: a fence that writes a fence-flagged query report is never
+        // skipped as empty. A skipped fence runs its operation at once, before the host GPU has run
+        // the work the report follows.
+        const bool delay_fence = VideoCore::g_signaling_query_report_fence ||
+                                 (Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorDefault()
+                                      ? Settings::IsGPULevelHigh()
+                                      : Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorBalanced() ||
+                                            Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate());
         if constexpr (!can_async_check) {
             TryReleasePendingFences<false>();
         }
diff --git a/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h b/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
index ac9a471..0121be1 100644
--- a/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include "video_core/query_cache/query_cache_base.h"
 #include "video_core/query_cache/query_stream.h"
 #include "video_core/query_cache/types.h"
+#include "video_core/rasterizer_interface.h"
 
 namespace VideoCommon {
 
@@ -272,7 +273,13 @@ void QueryCacheBase<Traits>::CounterReport(GPUVAddr addr, QueryType counter_type
     };
     u8* pointer = impl->device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(cpu_addr);
     u8* pointer_timestamp = impl->device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(cpu_addr + 8);
-    bool is_synced = (Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorDefault() ? !Settings::IsGPULevelHigh() : !Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorBalanced() && !Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate()) && is_fence;
+    // EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1 (Lichii PR 337, Inc0rporate): a fence-flagged report stays
+    // registered until its fence runs, as at High accuracy, without making other fences wait.
+    static const bool keep_pending = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    bool is_synced = !keep_pending && (Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorDefault() ? !Settings::IsGPULevelHigh() : !Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorBalanced() && !Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate()) && is_fence;
     std::function<void()> operation([this, is_synced, streamer, query_base = query, query_location,
                                      pointer, pointer_timestamp, cpu_addr] {
         if (True(query_base->flags & QueryFlagBits::IsInvalidated)) {
@@ -305,7 +312,9 @@ void QueryCacheBase<Traits>::CounterReport(GPUVAddr addr, QueryType counter_type
         }
     });
     if (is_fence) {
+        VideoCore::g_signaling_query_report_fence = keep_pending;
         impl->rasterizer.SignalFence(std::move(operation));
+        VideoCore::g_signaling_query_report_fence = false;
     } else {
         if (!Settings::IsGPULevelHigh() && counter_type == QueryType::Payload) {
             if (has_timestamp) {
diff --git a/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h b/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
index bb45c5f..732517d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
+++ b/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
@@ -43,6 +43,11 @@ enum class LoadCallbackStage {
 };
 using DiskResourceLoadCallback = std::function<void(LoadCallbackStage, std::size_t, std::size_t)>;
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1: set while the query cache signals the fence that writes a
+/// fence-flagged report, so the fence manager makes that fence even when it is empty
+/// (FenceManager::SignalFence).
+inline thread_local bool g_signaling_query_report_fence = false;
+
 class RasterizerInterface {
 public:
     virtual ~RasterizerInterface() = default;
-- 
2.54.0

